---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
	title="Pricing · Tab"
	description="How Tab's pricing works, in full: free to run yourself, a free hosted plan, and paid plans that publish their exact formula."
>
	<h1>Pricing</h1>
	<p class="lede">The whole formula, up front. No app-store guessing, no surprise bills.</p>

	<p class="note">
		<strong>Hosted plans aren't open yet,</strong> and the dollar amounts aren't set. This page shows
		exactly how they'll be worked out. The amounts will be published here before anyone can sign
		up.
	</p>

	<h2>On every plan</h2>
	<ul class="plain">
		<li>Log as many expenses as you like. No daily limits.</li>
		<li>Full history, balances, and settling up.</li>
		<li>Export all your data to a spreadsheet, any time.</li>
		<li>Ask from Claude Code or Claude Desktop, on your own Claude plan.</li>
		<li>No ads. We never sell your data.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>The plans</h2>
	<div class="shelf shelf--pairs">
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Run it yourself</h3>
			<p><strong>Free, forever.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Everything Tab does, on your own computer or server. Want it to read your bills? Add your
				own AI key and pay the AI company directly.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Hosted free</h3>
			<p><strong>$0. No card needed.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Everything except bill reading, hosted by us. Want bill reading? Add your own AI key, same as
				running it yourself.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Plus</h3>
			<p><strong>For people in lots of groups.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Hosting and bill reading included. Have as many groups as you like (a house, a club, a
				trip) on one plan, sharing one monthly reading allowance.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Pro</h3>
			<p><strong>For landlords and anyone billing other households.</strong></p>
			<p class="muted">
				Everything in Plus, and: see what each household owes you (or you owe them) in one place, pay
				back repair costs from there, and split one bill across several properties. Your households
				don't pay anything.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<h2>How Plus and Pro are charged</h2>
	<p>Each month, you pay whichever is lower:</p>
	<ul class="plain">
		<li>a flat monthly fee, or</li>
		<li>
			what reading your bills actually cost us that month, plus <strong>10%</strong> on Plus or{' '}
			<strong>8%</strong> on Pro.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>If that comes to less than $3, we don't charge you for that month.</p>

	<h2>When you reach your reading allowance</h2>
	<p>
		Each paid plan includes a monthly allowance of bills read for you. We tell you before you reach
		it. When you do, reading pauses until next month. You can still type expenses in yourself;
		nothing else stops.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you'd rather keep reading, you can turn on <strong>extra reading</strong>. It's off unless you
		switch it on. Extra bills cost the same as above (our cost plus 10% on Plus, plus 8% on Pro), and
		you set a monthly spending limit. Reach that limit and reading pauses, same as before. You're
		never charged past the limit you chose.
	</p>

	<h2>Why it's priced this way</h2>
	<p>
		Hosting Tab costs very little per household. Reading bills with AI is the cost that actually
		grows. So we add a small, fixed margin on that, and you never pay more than the flat fee. Tab is
		also free software: if a plan doesn't suit you, you can run the same thing yourself, for free,
		with your data.
	</p>
</Page>
